## Link 2: Contentstack Custom Preview URLs

**URL:** https://www.contentstack.com/docs/headless-cms/custom-preview-urls#configure-custom-preview-urls
**Posted by:** V-EPAM-Ivan Mikhailov, 2026-07-27
**Classification:** Vendor documentation — RELEVANT
**Fetch status:** Successfully fetched (HTTP 200)

### Document scope

This guide covers configuring custom, pattern-based preview URLs for Live Preview and Visual Editor. It is not architecture-specific (no mention of CSR/SSR/App Router/Pages Router). It is a configuration guide for Contentstack's UI.

### What the document says (quoted)

**Plan availability constraint:**
> "Custom Preview URLs is available on select plans. Contact Contentstack support for more information."

**What it does:**
> "Custom Preview URLs allow you to define dynamic, pattern-based paths for Live Preview. These paths align preview behavior with your website's routing logic, including nested routes, taxonomies, multiple domains, and non-native URL fields."

**Configuration is done in Contentstack UI (not code):**
> "Go to your stack and click 'Settings'. Navigate to Visual Experience and select the Preview URL tab. Enable the Custom Preview URL toggle."

**Pattern syntax uses `{{...}}` placeholders:**
> Entry fields: `{{entry.slug}}, {{entry.title}}, {{entry.uid}}`
> Context variables: `{{environment}}, {{locale}}, {{branch}}, {{contentTypeUid}}`
> Reference fields: `{{entry.author.name}}, {{entry.parent.url}}`
> Taxonomy values: `{{taxonomy:brand}}`

**One code requirement for Visual Editor only:**
> "To open the correct entry, the Start editing button passes the entry UID and content type UID as page context. Configure this context once in your front-end code. For setup steps, refer to setPageContext(context) in the Live Preview Utils SDK config reference."

**Fallback behavior:**
> "Reverts to the default preview URL if resolution fails."

### Relevance to story

The story covers GO, UP, and MX sites with different URL structures. Custom Preview URLs support *"multiple domains or regional sites"* and *"nested or hierarchical routing"*, which is directly relevant if the sites have different routing patterns. However, the plan availability constraint (*"available on select plans"*) should be verified with Contentstack — if the current plan doesn't include it, this feature cannot be used.

